# name: Tomas
Halfway over, a lantern swings on the far jetty. Soldiers, by the way it moves.
Tomas sees it too. He has gone very still.
"They're looking for me. I walked away from a war that isn't mine. If they find me, they'll hang me on the bridge they open tomorrow." # speaker: tomas
* [Hide him under the sailcloth.]
  # fx: set-flag(flag: tomas-hidden, to: true)
  He folds himself into the bow and you pile the sailcloth on top. It looks like sailcloth. It looks like nothing else at all.
* ["I can't help you."]
  # fx: set-flag(flag: tomas-alone, to: true)
  "No," he says. "I know." # speaker: tomas
  He takes his coat off and folds it, as though that will help.
- The lantern on the jetty stops swinging, and waits.
-> END
